<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Central Sudan</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sudan">Sudan</a> is the part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sahel">Sahel</a> and savanna belt of West and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/central-africa">Central Africa</a> between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/niger-bend">Niger bend</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lake-chad">Lake Chad</a>, in the historical sense of the Bilad al-Sudan. It was the home of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hausa">Hausa city-states</a> and of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kanem-bornu-empire">Kanem-Bornu</a>. The region was dominated by the Kanem-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bornu">Bornu Empire</a> and, from the nineteenth century, by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sokoto-caliphate">Sokoto Caliphate</a>.</p></div>
